{#- Landing hero (REQ-009; plan D-10, D-11; founder feedback round 1,
    si-yp2x): eyebrow, the page's only h1 (a U+2060 word joiner inside
    "AI-powered" keeps it on one line), the lead, the primary CTA — since
    feedback round 1 an anchor to the apps section (#apps in apps.njk), the
    site promotes what exists rather than "Start a project" — and the
    secondary CTA for nivå: while
    site.nivaUrl is null it is an honest early-access mailto:, once the
    founder sets the URL it links there and reads "Try nivå" with no template
    change. Then the proof line and the console: an honest log of this
    factory's build stages, every line a string, rendered as a three-column
    subgrid (stage | text | state) with the caret on the last line. It carries
    no times (si-qr13): the timed record of that run is the "build" figure in
    "Why we run an agent-run software factory", which names its clock (UTC)
    and gives each stage the time it closed. Stagger indices come from the
    :nth-child rules in base.css. -#}
{%- set hero = strings[lang].hero -%}
{%- set console = strings[lang].console -%}
<section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
  <div class="hero-glow" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="container hero-grid">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow reveal"><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>{{ hero.eyebrow }}</p>
      <h1 id="hero-title" class="reveal">{{ hero.title }}</h1>
      <p class="lead reveal">{{ hero.lead }}</p>
      <p class="cta-row reveal">
        <a class="button button-primary" href="#apps">{{ hero.ctaPrimary }}<span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        {%- if site.nivaUrl %}
        <a class="button button-secondary" href="{{ site.nivaUrl }}">{{ hero.nivaTry }}</a>
        {%- else %}
        <a class="button button-secondary" href="{{ hero.nivaEarlyAccessSubject | mailtoSubject }}">{{ hero.nivaEarlyAccess }}</a>
        {%- endif %}
      </p>
      <ul class="proof-list reveal">
        {%- for key, item in hero.proof %}
        <li><span class="plus" aria-hidden="true">+</span>{{ item }}</li>
        {%- endfor %}
      </ul>
    </div>
    <figure class="console reveal" aria-label="{{ console.ariaLabel }}">
      <div class="console-bar">
        <span class="console-dots" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span>
        <span class="console-title">{{ console.title }}</span>
      </div>
      <ol class="console-log">
        {%- for key, line in console.lines %}
        <li class="log-line"><span class="log-stage">{{ line.stage }}</span><span class="log-text">{{ line.text }}</span>{% if loop.last %}<span class="log-wait">{{ line.state }}<span class="caret" aria-hidden="true"></span></span>{% else %}<span class="log-ok">{{ line.state }}</span>{% endif %}</li>
        {%- endfor %}
      </ol>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>
